journey: feed/react-and-reply
expect-fail: S2

A reply whose quote can be jumped to (the quoted root is on screen, so the quote is a Button) loses the quote identifier, as if the GIF reply posted without its quote. S2.3 expects comment-quote-<id> on the new row, so it must fail.
scripts/qa/journey.py mutants applies this, runs the test, and reverts it.

diff --git a/apps/mobile/Monaco/Features/Comments/CommentQuote.swift b/apps/mobile/Monaco/Features/Comments/CommentQuote.swift
--- a/apps/mobile/Monaco/Features/Comments/CommentQuote.swift
+++ b/apps/mobile/Monaco/Features/Comments/CommentQuote.swift
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
         if quote.canJump {
             Button(action: onJump) { line }
                 .buttonStyle(.plain)
-                .accessibilityIdentifier("comment-quote-\(rowID)")
+                .accessibilityIdentifier("comment-cite-\(rowID)")
         } else {
             line.accessibilityIdentifier("comment-quote-\(rowID)")
         }
